From 517c69841488020d956980ce0956413e191a7396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaxorcist <vaxorcist@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:22:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SCP, HK: Common SDL2 sound support (sim_sound) and the RK07
 sound pilot

Sound for all simulators (sim_sound.c/.h), phases A and B:

- sim_sound is compiled into every simulator.  With SDL2 (USE_SIM_SOUND)
  it plays WAV samples through its own SDL audio device; without SDL2
  every playback call is a no-op while SET/SHOW SOUND, the realism flag
  and the power state still work.
- Mixer in the SDL audio callback: 64 voices, float summing with -6 dB
  headroom, soft limiter, master and group volumes (SYSTEM, DISK, TAPE,
  EVENT) with mutes, click-free fades, one-shot to loop chaining and
  random-phase loops.  Playback requests only queue a command.
- System sounds: RUN and BOOT power on (starting sound, running loop);
  stops at the prompt keep the power on; EXIT plays the stopping sound
  and waits, SET SOUND POWER=OFF switches off by hand.
- SET SOUND ENABLED switches on the realism mode (refused while a disk or
  tape is attached; disabled by default), including a per-simulator
  realistic THROTTLE unless the user set one (sim_timer: sim_throt_is_set).
- Unit loops for spindles, optional samples, file search in SET SOUND
  PATH, SIMH_SOUND_PATH, sound/<sim>/ beside or above the executable and
  ./sound/<sim>/.
- RK611 (HK): SET HKn ONLINE/OFFLINE (RUN/STOP buttons), SHOW HKn
  SPINDLE; in the realism mode ATTACH waits for ONLINE, spin-up time
  (SPINUP), UNLOAD spins down instead of detaching, realistic RK06/RK07
  seek, latency and transfer times, short/medium/long seek sounds
  (SEEK6S/SEEK6M/SEEK7S/SEEK7M), optional spindle sounds.
- Default sounds (per file, an own file wins): sound/default_cpu/ with
  recordings of a real VAX-11/750 (power relay and blower start, running
  blower as a seamless loop, power off and run-down), used by simulators
  that opt in (the vax750, also THROTTLE 300K, provisional);
  sound/default_disk/: synthetic seek sounds for every disk drive.  All
  sounds under the SIMH license.
- Builds: makefile (SDL2 audio for all simulators, NOSOUND=1), CMake
  (WITH_SOUND, simh_sound), descrip.mms.  The Visual Studio
  projects are not updated yet (they do not build sim_sound.c).

VMS boot fixes: the RK611 converts realistic durations to instructions
itself (at the throttle target rate), the realism mode starts the
throttle at power-on (THROT_DELAY 0), and the throttle measures freshly
with THROT_DELAY 0 (sim_timer: sim_throt_target_ips, sim_throt_set_delay).

Spin-up: SPINUP ms of simulated time while the CPU runs, wall time while
stopped at the sim> prompt (sim_sound run hooks); kept across RUN/BOOT and
controller clears.  Power on restores the spindle loops silenced by power
off.

SET HKn ONLINE/OFFLINE at the prompt wait until the drive is up to speed
or at rest (SPINUP, SPINDOWN); SET -N returns at once.

Common spindle support for removable-media disks (sim_spindle_*, own
timers, wall time at the prompt, waiting), used by the RK611 and the
RL11: RL01/RL02 realism mode with ONLINE/LOAD and OFFLINE/UNLOAD as the
LOAD button (40 s / 30 s), realistic RL seek and transfer times, seek sounds (rl02,
default_disk).

Massbus disks (RP): RUN/STOP button for the removable-pack drives,
realistic times per drive type (rotation speed, fitted seek curve),
seek sounds per drive type (default_disk).

MSCP disks (RQ): the RA60, the only removable-pack drive of the RA
series, gets the RUN/STOP button (SET RQn ONLINE/OFFLINE, offline-no-
volume while stopped, available attention when up to speed), AVAILABLE
with spin-down spins it down in the realism mode, realistic RA60 times
and seek sounds (ra60, default_disk).  SHOW RLn SPINDLE ends its line.

RB730 (VAX-11/730): the RB02 (an RL02) gets the LOAD button and the
realism mode (stopped drive: not ready, drive and spin error, so VMS sees
the medium offline), realistic RB02 and RB80 times, seek sounds (rl02
and rm80, default_disk).

MSCP disks (RQ), RC25: the removable RC25 and the fixed RCF25 (next
unit) share one spindle and one actuator.  SET RQn ONLINE/OFFLINE on
either unit is the Run button; in the realism mode the drive does not
start without a cartridge, spin-up 60 s / spin-down 30 s (SPINUPRC25,
SPINDOWNRC25), realistic RC25 times (2850 rpm, seek 10/35/55 ms, 31 ms
per track) and seek sounds (rc25, default_disk); a realistic configuration is
required (RC25 pairs with even/odd unit numbers on a KLESI, which only
connects RC25 drives), AVAILABLE with spin-down stops the whole drive,
KLESI controller timeout 15 s and ABORT of queued commands only.  RC25
geometry 31 x 2 x 821 in both modes.  sim_sound: no fixed limit on the
number of spindles, unit loops and run hooks; SET SOUND ENABLED
configuration checks of devices.

Tapes (TS): the TS11 (Unibus, TS04 transport, 45 in/s start/stop) and
the TSV05 (Qbus, TS05 transport, 25 in/s streaming) get an operator
panel (SET TS LOAD/ONLINE/OFFLINE/REWIND/UNLOAD, SET TS REEL=600|1200|
2400, SHOW TS TRANSPORT); in the realism mode ATTACH only mounts the
reel, motion commands, rewinds, loads and unloads take their real time,
a subsystem initialize rewinds in real time, EOT comes from the physical
position on the reel.  sim_sound: tape transports (SND_REEL), realtime
timers shared with the spindles, voices with playback rate glides,
delays and lifetimes; synthetic default tape sounds (default_tape) and
TSV05 sounds (tsv05).  In the realism mode SHOW TS shows the reel
instead of CAPACITY, and a forward motion beyond the recorded data moves
25 ft of blank tape before OPI.

TK50 cartridge streamer (TQ, sound realism mode): the TQK50 (Qbus) and
TUK50 (Unibus) drive gets a streamer model (sim_sound SND_STREAMER):
75 in/s, 45 KB/s, 22 serpentine tracks of 600 ft, a 32 KB buffer between
host and tape, the reposition cycle of a slow host (stop, back up 60 in,
start again), track turns, rewind at 80 in/s, EOT at the end of the 22nd
track.  ATTACH inserts the cartridge; SET TQn LOAD (the Load/Unload
button) loads in a random 10-15 s, plus 2 min of calibration for a new
(empty) cartridge; the host's unload and SET TQn UNLOAD rewind and
unload (9 s), the file stays attached; SHOW TQn TRANSPORT.  Synthetic
TK50 sounds (tk50) shaped after a TZ30 recording.  The TK70, TU81 and
TKUSER keep the old behaviour.  MicroVAX II: THROTTLE 450K in the
realism mode (provisional).  sim_sound_activate_us replaces an existing
activation (an asynchronous I/O completion has activated the unit
already).

TQ: a position command that runs beyond the recorded data (end of
medium, e.g. a DIRECTORY of a tape with an interrupted BACKUP) ends
with a data error instead of stopping the simulator with an I/O error.

Streamer sounds crossfade: a start ends with the loop's own beginning,
a stop fades in while the loop fades out; the TK50 motion sounds are
tonal (457 Hz with harmonics, little noise).

TQ: a position command into an invalid record or a format error ends
with the tape error instead of stopping the simulator.  Realism mode: a
new cartridge gets an end-of-medium marker after its calibration.
sim_tape: after an invalid record length the position is the record's
start again (was 2 GB off for a marker with bit 31 set).
sim_timer: the throttle without warm-up (realism mode) repeats an
unusable measurement instead of disabling the throttle, and its
recalibration no longer loops forever without a peak rate.

Streamers: SHOW TRANSPORT shows where the tape is during a rewind or
move.  TK50: the reverse of a reposition is audible (501 Hz, a 600 Hz
whine, hiss) after a short standstill.  VAX: CPU register STRSHIFT
(time charged for string instructions; default unchanged).

MSCP disks (RQ), the fixed RA drives RA70, RA71, RA72, RA73, RA80, RA81,
RA82, RA90 and RA92: each has a RUN/STOP switch like the RA60 and gets
its realism mode (SET RQn ONLINE/OFFLINE, ATTACH waits for ONLINE,
AVAILABLE with spin-down spins down, SPINUPRAnn/SPINDOWNRAnn), realistic
times from the published rotation speed and seek times, and seek sounds
per type (ra70 ... ra92, default_disk; SEEKRAnnS/SEEKRAnnM).
In the realism mode SDI drives (RA, ESE, RA8U) are only accepted on a
UDA50, UDA50A (Unibus only) or KDA50 (Qbus only), with at most 4
drives there.  RA80_LBN 237212
explained: a real RA80 reports it (User Guide: 236,964).
Start times from the drive User Guides: RA81 20 s, RA80 40 s.

Floppy disks (sim_sound SND_FLOPPY), first the RX02 (RY): the drive
mechanics give the timing and the sounds in the realism mode: AC spindle
motors that run while the power is on (H771 power supply), head load
solenoid with unload 200 ms after the last command, 6 ms per track,
25 ms settle, the sector under the head at its real time (the software's
interleave has its real effect), Initialize, Set Media Density (about
15 s), Read Status, buffer transfers at 1.2 us per bit; ATTACH/DETACH
are the door, a command on a drive whose door is opened ends with an
error.  Mixer: repeated one-shots (the step clicks).  Sounds in
sound/rx02 and the defaults in sound/default_floppy (synthetic).  Set
Media Density on an empty drive no longer crashes SIMH.  RY debug flags
OPS (realistic times), CMD (functions, INIT, completions with status)
and REG (register accesses).
Read Status sets the density error when the diskette density differs
from the function density (VMS DYDRIVER finds double density diskettes
that way; before, VMS MOUNT failed with DRVERR), and RX2CS Error reports
errors of the current function only.
The RX01 (RX device of the PDP-11 and the VAX-11/780 console floppy CS)
with the timing of the RX01 maintenance manual (10 ms per track, head
load after the steps and 20 ms, head unload after 46 ms, Read Status one
to two revolutions, 18 us per byte); it uses the RX02 sounds (same drive
mechanics) unless sound/rx01 has its own.  RX: SHOW RXn DRIVE, debug
flags OPS/CMD/REG, HELP RX; CS: SHOW CS DRIVE, debug flag OPS, HELP CS.

This patch applies on top of opensimh_6_rb730 (the RB730 fixes); it
also applies after the DMV11, DMF32, VAX 8200 and DMC patches (1-4).

